  "description": "Native-precision DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash on four RTX PRO 6000 Blackwell cards with 125 GiB of host RAM, using Local Inference Lab vLLM jovian-judgement r38 unchanged: TP4, B12X attention/MoE/linear, FP8 KV, DSpark K7 with adaptive verification, vision, 524,288 context, 4096 batched tokens, 16 sequences, breakable CUDA graphs. Engram tables are read from disk with io_uring, so the host does not need the ~189 GiB that RAM mode pins; the container needs unlimited memlock and a seccomp profile that allows io_uring (Docker default plus three syscalls, shipped with the evidence). Boot reports a 7,636,766-token KV pool (14.57x at 524k). A cold 500,000-token prefill and eight concurrent cold 150,000-token prompts completed with flat GPU memory. Replaces the SGLang recipe on the same host, which hit CUDA OOM in the low-ratio indexer on cold prefills past about 290k tokens. Host GPUs are capped at 275 W without a P2P driver override, so decode is below Local Inference Lab's published r38 figures.",
